  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Hosea",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 11,
    "summary": "Israel, as a child, was called out of Egypt in similitude of our Lord, as a child, coming out of Egypt—But Ephraim turns away from the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "When Israel was a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG God, Love of."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Ex. 4:22 (22–23)."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Prophecies about."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As they called them, so they went from them: they sacrificed unto Baalim, and burned incense to graven images.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Hosea 13:1 (1–4)."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 17:16 (15–16); Hosea 2:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I taught Ephraim also to go, taking them by their arms; but they knew not that I healed them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "1 Ne. 17:41 (40–41); Alma 33:20 (18–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I drew them with cords of a man, with bands of love: and I was to them as they that take off the yoke on their jaws, and I laid meat unto them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Love."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall not return into the land of Egypt, but the Assyrian shall be his king, because they refused to return.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Hosea 8:13 (11–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sword shall abide on his cities, and shall consume his branches, and devour them, because of their own counsels.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "Hosea 10:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And my people are bent to backsliding from me: though they called them to the most High, none at all would exalt him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Ingratitude."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "Hosea 7:16 (14–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 117
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "How shall I give thee up, Ephraim? how shall I deliver thee, Israel? how shall I make thee as Admah? how shall I set thee as Zeboim? mine heart is turned within me, my repentings are kindled together.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "Gen. 19:24 (24–25); Deut. 29:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 160,
            "text": "JST Hosea 11:8 … toward thee, and my mercies are extended to gather thee."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will not execute the fierceness of mine anger, I will not return to destroy Ephraim: for I am God, and not man; the Holy One in the midst of thee: and I will not enter into the city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 164,
            "end": 169,
            "text": "OR come in anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They shall walk after the Lord: he shall roar like a lion: when he shall roar, then the children shall tremble from the west.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Isa. 31:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They shall tremble as a bird out of Egypt, and as a dove out of the land of Assyria: and I will place them in their houses, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ephraim compasseth me about with lies, and the house of Israel with deceit: but Judah yet ruleth with God, and is faithful with the saints.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "OR walks."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
